# goal A self-contained public distribution surface

`sites/git-a2a.com/` is the complete static package served at `https://git-a2a.com`: product
documentation, public schemas, the A2A extension description, and checksum-verifying installers.

# decision Site publication is automated but separate from CLI releases {#publication}

Pushes to `main` that change the static site or its canonical inputs run the dedicated site
workflow after `make site-check`; CLI tags and the release workflow never deploy the site. The
deployment job is additionally gated by the explicit repository variable `SITE_AUTO_DEPLOY=true`
and stays skipped until the dedicated deployment identity and protected environment are approved. The
workflow stages an explicit allowlist through `scripts/site-package.sh` and uploads that staging
directory with OpenSSH. Hosting account, endpoint, port, document root, private key, and host-key
material exist only as protected `site-production` environment secrets; workflow source and logs
must not reveal their values. Design sources, generators, operator documentation, and repository
metadata are never part of the upload.

Manual publication uses `make site-publish`, the same allowlist, and local OpenSSH. Its endpoint,
account, document root, and optional SSH paths come from the gitignored root `.env`; only an empty
`.env.example` is tracked. Manual publication must pass `site-check` before contacting the host.

The allowlist includes `.htaccess` because it is runtime configuration for the public surface:
Apache serves `.ps1` and `.sh` as `text/plain` with UTF-8 so PowerShell `Invoke-RestMethod` and
shell downloads receive text. Treat it as a deploy artifact, not a navigable route. Verify the
live PowerShell path only after manual publication, on `windows-latest`, by checking the response
Content-Type and compiling the exact `Invoke-RestMethod` response into a script block for a
`--dry-run`; a repository-only test cannot prove the host applied `.htaccess`.

# invariant Canonical files stay byte-identical {#canonical_files}

The public `install.sh` is byte-identical to the repository-root `install.sh` used by release
documentation. `schema/a2amodule.v1.json` and `schema/a2amodule-lock.v1.json` are byte-identical
to their respective files under `spec/schema/`. Checks fail on drift.

# decision Static, local-first implementation {#static_site}

The site uses hand-written HTML and one CSS and JavaScript file, with no framework, generator,
analytics, remote fonts, or runtime service. Every page renders from `file://` and an ordinary
static HTTP server. The only JavaScript behaviours are transcript replay, copy buttons, and
keyboard-accessible install tabs.
The `/spec/` reader page is the sole generated HTML exception: `tools/gen-spec-page.py`
deterministically escapes the exact bytes of `spec/README.md` and normative `spec/_.hint` into
the shared static page shell. It adds no runtime dependency and GitHub remains canonical for diffs.

# decision Visual source and static asset provenance {#visual_source}

`sites/design/README.md` is authoritative for copy, tokens, spacing, typography, and behaviour;
its prototypes are references, never production markup. IBM Plex Sans and JetBrains Mono are
pinned OFL WOFF2 assets. Wordmark glyphs are outlined by the committed CoreText generator,
size-specific favicons by ImageMagick, and social cards by the committed headless-Chrome template.

# invariant The transcript is real and accessible {#transcript}

`assets/transcript.json` contains real CLI stdout and stderr bytes from the repository's canonical
VERSION build against the public demo or
its byte-equivalent local bare fixture, including line endings and alignment spaces. The displayed
add command is exactly the public HTTPS demo command with no hidden flag; npm, uv, and Go resolve
and refresh against the local bare repository through process-scoped Git URL rewrites. The landing
embeds identical completed data
as its no-JavaScript and `file://` fallback. Output lines use `white-space: pre` and JetBrains Mono.
Reduced motion skips typing, replay clears every timer, and the terminal copy action returns only
the four commands. The site gate reruns `tools/transcript-generate.sh --check` and permits only the
resolved fixture commit hash to vary.
The transcript harness connects every captured command to a null stdin so terminal inheritance
cannot turn the visually unchanged `git-a2a init` command into an interactive session.

The public demo source is `neprel/git-a2a-demo-acme-lib` and its consumer is
`neprel/git-a2a-demo-acme-app`. `SITE_NET=1` reruns the transcript against those public GitHub
repositories without URL rewrites; the default site gate remains the byte-equivalent local bare
fixture so offline checks are deterministic. Static A2A v1.0 cards live under
`/demo/agents/<name>/.well-known/agent-card.json`, and `/.well-known/ai-catalog.json` lists exactly
those cards. Both path trees are explicit publication-allowlist entries. The cards demonstrate
discovery only and must say that their interface URLs do not run agent services. Each committed
card is the byte output of `git-a2a card export` in the demo library, so it carries the canonical
`https://git-a2a.com/ext/module/v1` binding; the catalog is likewise regenerated by `git-a2a
catalog export` rather than hand-edited.

# decision Search and machine discovery are static and canonical {#discovery}

Each public HTML page has one canonical URL, unique descriptive metadata, social-card metadata,
and Schema.org JSON-LD limited to facts asserted by the project. `sitemap.xml` lists the three
canonical HTML pages and `robots.txt` points to it; the 404 response is `noindex`. `llms.txt` is
a concise map to the canonical specification, CLI reference, schemas and extension, while
`llms-full.txt` is a self-contained factual overview for retrieval systems. Both are guidance,
not alternative specifications, and must not invent capabilities or override `spec/README.md`.
The Stripe-compatible `/.well-known/skills/index.json` lists the git-a2a Agent Skill and every
file needed to install it; `/.well-known/skills/git-a2a/` is byte-identical to
`skills/git-a2a/`. Markdown and JSON receive explicit MIME types. The site is a distribution copy,
not a second source: `tools/sync-skill.py` owns both the tree and index.
The structured data links to the moving Releases page and therefore does not carry a hand-maintained
`softwareVersion`; live channel checks, not mutable landing-page metadata, prove the current release.

# invariant Enumerable integration copy is generated

Counts and lists of native ecosystems, vendored build systems, agent harnesses, distribution
channels, contact kinds, and projected standards on the landing page come only from the checked
registry in `tools/gen-reference.py`. The same run updates the root README, `spec/README.md`, the
high-fidelity prototype, and the design handoff; `site-check` fails on any drift. Do not hand-edit
those marked blocks or repeat a numeric integration claim outside them.

# decision Release verification is workflow-identity based {#release_verification}

The landing page gives copyable verification commands for both forms of published output:
`gh attestation verify` binds a downloaded Release asset to the repository, and `cosign verify`
binds an immutable GHCR digest to the tag-triggered release workflow and GitHub's OIDC issuer.
The page must never ask for or imply a project-managed signing key. Visible verification copy is
also recorded in the design prototype so the existing node-parity check remains authoritative.

# build Site and installer checks

`make installers-check` parses and dry-runs the POSIX installer without network access. The
complete site gate is `make site-check`; it verifies synced files, HTML and links, duplicated
header/footer bytes, visible-copy parity with the design, discovery metadata, transcript facts,
content policy, and the transfer budget. With `SITE_BROWSER=1`, a pinned Playwright/Chromium suite
also checks mobile overflow, reduced motion, keyboard tabs, focus rings, and serious axe findings;
CI always enables that browser gate for site changes.
